A reload of the configuration while the session is locked made new lock
surfaces before taking over the old ones: the surfaces made ahead of the
lock were given no old instance, and those made after it, which were,
found the screens taken. The second surface for an output is a protocol
error (ext_session_lock_v1: duplicate_output), which ends the process
with the session locked.

--- a/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
+++ b/src/wayland/session_lock.cpp
@@ -146,7 +146,7 @@
 
 			// preload initial surfaces to make the chance of the compositor displaying a blank
 			// frame before the lock surfaces are shown as low as possible.
-			this->updateSurfaces(false);
+			this->updateSurfaces(false, old);
 
 			auto wasLocked = this->isLocked();
 			if (!this->manager->lock()) {
